{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you lend your neighbor.</b> This commandment was already stated: ״אם כסף תלוה את עמי״, and it is repeated here on account of ״בחוץ תעמוד״ etc., and to teach about a creditor that his law is with zaburit." "<b>Any pledge.</b> To include the wages of a hired worker and shop credit." "<b>Masha'at.</b> Written with alef and not read." "<b>You shall not come into his house.</b> Perhaps there is in it something requiring modesty."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:04.952816078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}